      <activity id="ecadfbc9-4fb0-5808-8a67-190d607fefd0" activityNameId="7ca80ada-3134-5218-b1bb-464c1353828c" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, ventilation equipment, KWL 250</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, ventilation equipment, KWL 250
Disposal of the ventilation unit for decentral ventilation systems with 120 m3/h average air flow. Housing made of galvanised steel insulated with rock wool. Heat recovery element made of aluminium. Total weight of component 40 kg;
UUID: 7274049c-3590-4dfa-9073-f5f05397997c
Transport to dismantling facilities, machines for handling in sorting plant, electricity demand for sorting plant, final disposal of waste material. Cut-off to recycling for metals.
Location: Specific to the technology mix encountered in sorting plants in Switzerland
Technology: Disposal to a sorting plant assumed. Metal pieces and copper in cables and electronic devices are recycled, plastic parts are incinerated, inert wastes (e.g. rock wool) are landfilled.
Time period: Amount of material investigated in 2003. Disposal technology mix as used in late 1990ies
Production volume: na
Sampling: Questionnaire and assumptions. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_7274049c-3590-4dfa-9073-f5f05397997c.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
